A||N||33||Cozmo||$10K Wonder Car?||||5||
Z||000000||Cozmo||10-28-2001||04:16 AM||||Viewing the current crop of European, Asian and American performance cars, can we build a Fiero that is in the same class for $10K (US).<BR>Assume you do most of the work yourself.<BR>It's got to look good and be comfortable.<BR>Be fast, reliable and safe.<BR>This has been discussed a lot, but what if you had to help someone put together a $10K package?<BR>Suggestions?<BR><P>------------------<BR><B>BobC</B><BR><B>'85 2M6 Targa</B><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/targsig.jpg"> <BR><B>Suncoast Fieros</B>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||10-28-2001||06:10 AM||||All depends on what you want to accomplish.  You should be able to get something that is reasonably quick, with decent handling and stay fairly comfortable for less than 10 grand.  But if you want to be really fast, handle with the best, etc, etc, you'll spend alot more $$.  I would think that alot of it would depend on what you start out with.  <P>I'll end up with 15 grand in mine before I'm through with it, but that will include a new motor (a V8 would be nice, but then I'd exceed my budget--who knows), custom interior, and some neat body mods in addition to a new suspension, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Screwie||10-28-2001||06:17 AM||||Well, from what I've heard, a Fiero is already very safe, so nothing there. The looks, well, even stock the Fiero looks amazing so it doesn't need much more to be up there with the other performance cars. So, fast, comfortable and reliable is what I'd put my money into if I had $10K. So, engine, suspension, interior, exhaust system and all that kind of stuff. Don't know the prices though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||10-28-2001||06:46 AM||||sounds doable to me. not literally 'cause i don't have enough mech. skills to do enough work myself to keep cost down. plus i'm not sure of suspension cost. <P>the most i've paid for a fiero is $2000, the least $125. any of them could potentially be the starting point for me. <BR>if you could use the $4000 minimum thread you've got smallblock v8 power for it. or spend more or less with the caddy swaps. if you thought the pre northstar caddy v8 was "exotic" enough and you could do it yourself you could potentially have the drivetrain sorted out with around $9000 still to do the rest.<P>if you found a relativly low mile ws6 car you might be able to get away with just lowering springs. i've done very little suspension work so i can't guess on those cost numbers. i guess if you went with some rayne pieces you'd bre spending some real cash.<P>style and comfort are personal things, but even if you did a budget smallblock swap and spent a couple thousand on suspension your still looking at $3-5000 to "spiff" up the car.<P>lots of "ifs" but it seems like it would be hard not to end up with something nice.<P>hey, who's spent about that much? where do you think you are and what do you think you have in comparision to newer and/or more exotic cars out there?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula||10-28-2001||10:23 AM||||Heres the body mods, wheels, tires, paint,  hood scoop, tailights (2nd picture). fog lights,and window tint <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FormulaRearscoop1.JPG">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/docu0012.jpg">  <P><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Formulafrontwheels1.JPG">  <P><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Stroker1.jpg">  <P>It will out run a new mustang gt and would probably handle with a most supercars.  And turns just as many heads!<P>It probably has around $7k in it. <p>[This message has been edited by Formula (edited 10-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||10-28-2001||10:49 AM||||A friend of mine picked up an 88 coupe for less than $100. It has decent paint, new headliner and A/C system so little would have to be spent on appearance and comfort. That leaves $9900, with an Archie kit, a warmed over v8 and upgraded brakes, it would be interesting to see what would happen.||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||10-28-2001||05:07 PM||||Mine's going to be close, but over the $10k mark a bit. I would put it with any production car made today.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000007||GTMike||10-28-2001||06:32 PM||||i plan to do it for alot less than 10k.  well my car cost 5k. it had 43k on it and is in show room condition. the only thing i would have to do is swap in a pushrod 3.4 for some more speed. figure 800 to 1000 for that and then some drop spindles for the front and some coil over for the back and the bumb stear kit.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">    <P>what kind of cars are you trying to compare it to?<P>------------------<BR>87GT mostly stock, cold air intake, no cat. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gtmike1_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||87FieroGTx||10-28-2001||09:08 PM|||| Fiero......  $1,000<P> Hot 3.1/3.4  $2,000<BR> (220hp)<P> NOS........  $600<BR> <BR> Full Konis     <BR> Suspension.  $1,000<P> Choptop....  $2,500<P> Interior...  $1,000<P> Big Brakes.  $500<P> Paint......  $500+<P> Side vents.  $200<P> 17" rims...  $600<P> Tires......  $500<P> <BR> With these mods you would look good, Do the quarter in low 13's and pull well over 1g on the skidpad.<P> All but the Choptop and Paint can be don't at home with basic tools, Building the engine may look hard but trust me with proper tools and good instructions it's not as hard as it seems.<P> This is enough to beat almost any car on the road today.<P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT ~ auto 3.2 200hp 220tq ~ 75 shot NOS ~ 0-60 4.8 13.9 1/4||||reg||4
Z||000009||pontiacs4me||10-28-2001||10:43 PM||||heres my figures<P>87 coupe w/blown 2.5 $500<P>L67 3800 series II supercharged <BR>w 4t65e transaxle $1694<P>engine rebuild parts $384<P>tranny rebuild kit $140<P>custom axles $400<P>custom computer system $700<P>1.9 rocker arms $300<P>ported heads, intake and blower $0<P>DIY headers $125<P>3" exhaust $50<P>install kit $50 worth of parts and a little ingenuity<P>lowering springs $160<P>17" rims and tires $1000<P>aprox $5300, bring it on viper!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Soon to be: L67 powered 87 coupe.||||reg||1
Z||000010||BlackStang95||10-29-2001||12:49 AM||||Are you talking 10k total or 10k invested?  10k invested I think it's possible, if the car was already in good shape, paint, rims/tires, and you were just doing engine swap, exhaust, clutch, suspension etc.  But to do everything you need to make an old fiero a new car its way more than 10k, you basically replace or repair everything but the chassis and transaxle.  My friend spek has a gt in decent shape and figured it would cost around 20k to do everything he wanted to it (doing work himself).  The best performance value for 10k (including car purchase price) has to be a mid 80's 5.0 mustang, these can be had in good shape for 3k, in great shape for 5k, and easily made to run deep into the 13's for 5k.  I'm speaking of strictly drag performance though, you might be looking for something else.<p>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 10-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||BlackStang95||10-29-2001||12:52 AM||||But you gotta remember, there's no new car you can by anywhere for 10k (maybe a kia?) much less a performance one.   ||||reg||1
Z||000012||87FieroGTx||10-29-2001||02:23 AM|||| If your comparing it to a new car you should up the budget to 25-30k <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> Ok.. Let me see!<P> Low mile<BR> 88FieroGT T-Top.. $5,000<P> Choptop........  $2,500<P> Longitudinal<BR> LS6/Zr1 V8......  $8,000-$10,000<BR> <BR> With<BR> <BR> Porsche 911 <BR> 5speed .........  $2,000<P> Custom Exhaust... $1,000<BR> <BR> Full Koni<BR> Suspension kit<BR> With 1 1/2" drop   $1,000<P> Full Polly<BR> Bushings........    $200<P> 13" Brakes.....   $1,000<P> 17" front <BR> 18" rear rims...... $600<P> P-zero tires....... $800<P> Sweet Paint job...  $1,500<BR> <BR> Paint Frame, Engine<BR> bay, under the hood. $100<BR> <BR> Leather and<BR> Brushed Aluminum<BR> Euro Interior<BR> 200mph speedo<BR> White face gages... $1,000<P> Nice CD/MP3 player<BR> Mega AMP..........  $1,000<P> Ausfiero Side scoops.. $250?<P> Euro Tail lights... $300<P> Remove Wing/badges<BR> fill in all <BR> "Pontiac's"........ $0-$10<P> Front battery <BR> relocation kit..... $100?<P> New radiator....... $500<P> replace every hose <BR> with braided steel.. $500?<P> Alarm, remote door/ <BR> hood/ Trunk opener..  $500<P> Wow that was actully hard to spend 30k<P> <P><BR> With this setup the stat's should be around,<P> 1/4 ~ 11.5 or quicker<P> 0-60 ~ 4.0<BR> <BR> 60-0 ~ 100 feet<P> Top speed ~ 190+<P> Skidpad ~ 1.4g<P> H-speed Slalom ~ 70mph+<P> This would pull away from/out handle any stock production car being made today!<P> In short for 30k you could Kill a 250,000 Diablo or hang with/kill a $1,000,000 Maclaren F1<BR><P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT ~ auto 3.2 200hp 220tq ~ 75 shot NOS ~ 0-60 4.8 13.9 1/4||||reg||4
Z||000013||GTMike||10-29-2001||02:48 AM||||it all depends on what kind of car you compare it to.  what foreign cars are we talking about. eclips? RX7? supra?  or a honda civic or a integra?  <P>do we need to run 13 second 1/4s or do we need low 15s.  <P>i say 3800 sc to get in 13s<BR>and the 3400 tdc for low 14s  <P>500-600 bucks on suspension<P>my car doesn't need paint  except to get rid of the ugly gray ground affects.<P>my interior is perfect as is.<P>maybe some 17" wheels and some cool tires.<P>i dont need a chop top. <P>these are just things that i would do to get it to be just as good as a new $20k foreign car.  as is we can handle just as well and can run mid 15s in the 1/4.  i say my 50K mile fiero is just as good as it sits in my driveway.||||reg||1
