Z||000019||87FieroGTx||10-29-2001||03:31 PM|||| ""The best performance value for 10k (including car purchase price) has to be a mid 80's 5.0 mustang, these can be had in good shape for 3k, in great shape for 5k, and easily made to run deep into the 13's for 5k.  I'm speaking of strictly drag performance though"" Posted by BS95<P><BR> I would have to disagree with you on that one!<P> You could go out and get a nice 70 Chevelle SS (any muscle car will do) for $3,000 get some sticky tires $500 hey guess what? I'm doing 12's. Performance rebuild the 454 $1,500 Hmm.. I'm in the low 11's add a supercharger $2,000 Wow I'm in the 10's, 200hp+ shot of NOS $1,000 and your close to 9's if not quicker. I did this back in my teens all for under 5k my fastest ET was 10.3 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR> I'm speaking of strictly drag performance though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT ~ auto 3.2 200hp 220tq ~ 75 shot NOS ~ 0-60 4.8 13.9 1/4<p>[This message has been edited by 87FieroGTx (edited 10-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||BlackStang95||10-29-2001||06:05 PM||||You'd need a lot more than tires to get those times.  A stock 70 chevelle ss with the highest factory engine (454) got 0-60 in low 6's, 1/4's in high 13's.  Not to mention what those cars in good shape cost these days.  <p>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 10-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||87FieroGTx||10-29-2001||06:52 PM|||| BS95 DO YOU HAVE ONE? NO <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> The reason they did high 13's is the POS Tires from that era, And the tires they came with were thin.<P> Go buy some real 60's tires put them on your car and they will add a second or more to your 1/4<P> All they need to get to 12 are Wide Slicks/good tires and maybe lighten them up and that's free. You can take a good 600lbs off them easy 1,000 If you don't care about comfort.<P> I see 65-72 Nice (not Mint) but Nice Muscle cars all the time for less than 2k <P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT ~ auto 3.2 200hp 220tq ~ 75 shot NOS ~ 0-60 4.8 13.9 1/4||||reg||1
