Z||000024||AutoXdbdragSE||10-29-2001||10:59 PM||||here we go again...<BR>blackstang just give up, you won't convince him..<BR>for 10k, any older car can be made to keep up with moder cars.<BR>my choice, is and will be a 89 supra turbo..<BR>stock 0-60 6.6 1/4mile 14.5<BR>around 7k for a perfect car..<BR>put 2k of engine work, and 1k in tires and you will have a great handling 5 second 0-60 car with 1/4 mile of sub 13.5 put it on the bottle and where talking 4.2-4.6 0-60 and sub(way sub) 13 quarters<BR>you could also build a nice mustang for 10k.. yes even good handling.. 10k is alot of money when you consider out of that 10k 3-7k is all perfomance mods.  If you think about it, the fiero isn't a cheap car to make fast.  the stock 2.8 isn't the best, with the exception of NOS there isn't much cheap power to be had. handling is good, but any serious improvment.. like .5 g or more is gonna cost some serious dollars.. big performance gains all come from nice expensive engine swaps.. if you want to compare apples to apples.. blackstang is right.. throw a Built 460 into a 80's 5.0 for &lt;1500, and blow the rest of the money on handleing alone, and i don't think you could build  a fiero for 10k that could keep up.  But this is just my .02c, and what do i know, i just have a iron duke fiero<P>------------------<BR>Bahh.. V-6, who needs it.. i got me some 4.10's<P>[URL <A HREF="http://www.sounddomain.com/id/dbdrag2]SEE" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sounddomain.com/id/dbdrag2]SEE</A>  MY CAR, 84 fiero hittin 147.5DBs[/URL]||||reg||1
Z||000025||ffindley||10-29-2001||11:25 PM||||I have been doing an analysis on this very topic as $10K is what I plan to spend in total on my Formula.  I have been looking at the new model year of sports cars and comparing a stock formula and other options to them.  Right now, I only have independently confirmed data for the stock Formula and an 88 GT 3.1 w/Turbo (Miller Woods setup).<P>Interesting to note that just the stroking and the Turbo puts you in very good company, though not into the exotics.  For that, you will need more horsepower. Does anyone have verified data on other conversions such as N*, Caddy, 3.4, CSB, 3800, etc?  I am looking for actual tested numbers, not hypotheticals.<P>Below are some of the charts showing price and performance.  Hopefully they will load in quickly as they are compressed pretty small.  (I apologize if they take too long).<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Price.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Acceleration.JPG"> <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/QuarterMileTime.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/QuarterMileSpeed.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TopSpeed.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Road_Handling.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Horsepower.JPG"> <P>-----------------<BR>1988 Yellow Formula Fiero<P>[This message has been edited by ffindley (edited 10-29-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by ffindley (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||3
